# .github/ was previously ignored ("due to API permissions"), which meant the
# repository could not have CI at all. That gap is why a broken migration, 20
# tables of schema drift, inert RLS policies and a crash-on-boot logger all
# reached main unnoticed. The directory is now tracked.
#
# The pipeline lives at .github/workflows-staged/ci.yml rather than
# .github/workflows/ because the token used by this automation is a GitHub App
# without `workflows` permission, so pushes touching .github/workflows/ are
# rejected outright. Run `bash .github/install-workflows.sh` from an account
# that has the permission to activate it. See .github/README.md.

